Spec: Held-socket private stream adapter

Purpose:
  Supply a real Java TCP socket to standard TLS/HTTP libraries over a private gateway stream.

Owns:
  ./SocketAdapter.java

Must:
  Close the application endpoint before the bridge peer on abort so an interrupted descriptor is not deliberately converted into a clean peer FIN.
  Keep the loopback listener transient and private to setup; match both endpoints to the already-held connected socket.
  Reject unmatched contenders before reading or forwarding their bytes and bound acceptance to two seconds.
  Preserve each direction's EOF and backpressure with at most two bounded copy workers per stream.
  On setup rejection, cancellation or failed pumps, close both socket endpoints and the underlying descriptor.
  Closing the application socket immediately aborts the descriptor and blocked copy workers; output half-close alone preserves inbound delivery.
